1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,810
Rishi Samvanana's whole
assembly was fighting…

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:05,959
and the fire between them
began to die.

3
00:00:06,379 --> 00:00:08,009
The Rigveda's last hymn…

4
00:00:08,009 --> 00:00:10,759
Sangachadhvam.
Its real meaning…

5
00:00:10,759 --> 00:00:12,534
very few people know.

6
00:00:12,964 --> 00:00:14,164
One says—

7
00:00:14,164 --> 00:00:17,815
"Water to our fields first!"
The other— "No, ours!"

8
00:00:17,845 --> 00:00:19,575
Like a family fight…

9
00:00:19,575 --> 00:00:22,490
everyone's talking,
no one is listening.

10
00:00:22,890 --> 00:00:24,550
Then the rishi stands…

11
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:27,520
and says just one word— Sam.

12
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:29,988
Walk together, speak together,

13
00:00:29,988 --> 00:00:32,866
let your minds
understand one another.

14
00:00:33,876 --> 00:00:34,926
It means…

15
00:00:34,926 --> 00:00:37,406
walk together, speak together…

16
00:00:37,406 --> 00:00:39,414
and understand
each other's minds.

17
00:00:39,434 --> 00:00:41,394
"Sam" means together…

18
00:00:41,394 --> 00:00:43,624
"Jānatām" means understand…

19
00:00:43,624 --> 00:00:46,291
"Everyone think alike"… it
never says that.

20
00:00:46,411 --> 00:00:48,331
It's said to the
whole assembly…

21
00:00:48,331 --> 00:00:50,703
so that all may
live well together.

22
00:00:51,213 --> 00:00:55,340
Slowly, everyone sits down…
and the fire burns bright
again.

23
00:00:55,870 --> 00:00:58,640
In your next argument… before
you reply, ask—

24
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,251
"Is this what you mean?"

25
00:01:00,751 --> 00:01:04,013
Tell us in the comments… who
listens first in your home?

26
00:01:04,353 --> 00:01:06,463
Because before we
speak together…

27
00:01:06,463 --> 00:01:08,245
we have to listen together.
